brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net make a bluesky feed that only includes posts that do  not contain the letters a/A or i/I in any combination or in any word

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@proptermalone.bsky.social: i think there's a kernel of truth that the benefits of LLMs have mostly accrued to spreadsheet people because spreadsheet people are the most likely early adopters of agentic LLMs
@proptermalone.bsky.social: as i've said before though i don't think there's going to be a huge difference in the long run between getting onboard early and getting on board late.  there's not really a huge learning curve for most applications, just by the nature of the thing.
@proptermalone.bsky.social: if you never use 'em then yeah you're not going to see some direct benefits that people using them see.  sorry.
@proptermalone.bsky.social: i am reasonably confident that i could figure out a way any person on Bluesky could use a $20 OpenAI or Claude subscription to improve some aspect of their life in fifteen minutes of talking through it, if they're willing to try in good faith
